===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# An ancient Roman family name, notably that of [[w:Julius Caesar|Gaius Iulius Caesar]].
# {{context|figuratively|lang=en}} The government; society; earthly powers.
#* {{RQ:Authorized Version|Matthew|22|21}}:
#*: Render therefore unto '''Caesar''' the things which are '''Caesar'''’s; and unto God the things that are God's.
#* {{quote-book|title=The past and present life of the globe|page=9|books.google.com/books?id=LjwDAAAAQAAJ|author=David Page|year=1861|passage=let it be clearly understood that we are dealing with Life solely in its geological aspects. We appeal unto '''Caesar'''; let us be judged by '''Caesar''''s laws.|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=LjwDAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA9&dq=%22Caesar%27s+laws%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Py3jUfTbNofa4AOQ_ICoAg&ved=0CJABEOgBMBE4eA#v=onepage&q=%22Caesar%27s%20laws%22&f=false}}
#* {{quote-journal|journal=Awake|volume=38|issue=14|page=6|books.google.com/books?id=bsAEAAAAYAAJ|year=1957|passage='''Caesar''' may discriminate unjustly against certain races. Christians are not to take issue with '''Caesar''''s laws on such matters and flout them, but should submit.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=On Doing Local History|page=76|books.google.com/books?isbn=0759102538|author=Carol Kammen|year=2003|passage=It is the story of churches that split apart over this issue and of ministers finding ways to justify the return of slaves because they were under the aegis of the laws of '''Caesar''', not the laws of God.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=God Is My Broker|books.google.com/books?isbn=0307799557|author=Christopher Buckley|year=2012|passage=But I know that '''Caesar''''s laws have been broken, and someone has to pay. I'm your man. These are good monks. If they committed any crime, it was to believe in me.|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=OrEoO6eiIvcC&pg=PT204&dq=%22Caesar%27s+laws%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=LizjUZ6zKrPI4APgloBI&ved=0CDoQ6AEwATha}}

